# Rover P5 3-Litre four-door saloon, 1958-1967.
#
# The first P5: the wide, low four-door with the 3.0-litre six, the upright
# grille and the roofline that carried into the P5B. The pack photographs a
# Mk I car; the Mk II and Mk III noses are not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P5
#
# Dimensions 4.737 x 1.778 x 1.549 m, wheelbase 2.807 m (Mk I basis).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is NOT level and is identified as a July 1960 Mk I
# by its date and 2,995 cc engine. The rear photograph's exact mark is
# uncertain. The flank is estimated from the three views and the published
# dimensions; the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: no model-specific UK chart was established at the time of the
# pack. Arden Green, Sierra Beige, Mexico Brown and Black are documented
# Rover finishes of the period. Weights 30, 26, 24, 20, total 100,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 165 km/h. Comfort 80/450, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 80. Class 3.
# Dates are road presence: 1958 intro, retires staggered 1982-1985.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-p5-3litre.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-p5-3litre.dae. References:
# citycars/references/rover-p5-3litre/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: image 1 is a tilted July 1960 Mk I, not a scaling
# elevation. The roof corners and rear glass are too angular, and the grille,
# headlamps and bumper ends need closer fitting. The Mk III trim in image 4 was
# not copied to the Mk I. At 128 px the wide low P5 body and Mk I nose read as a
# P5 3-Litre.


obj=citycar
name=RoverP53Litre(ArdenGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=30
intro_year=1958
intro_month=9
retire_year=1985
retire_month=6
speed=165
length=3
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=80
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=450

